    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "How much is it?",
     "texto": [
      "**¿Cuánto cuesta?** is for one thing. **¿Cuánto cuestan?** is for more than one.\n\n**Quiero** esta camisa. In **querer**, the **e** changes to **ie**: **quiero, quieres, quiere, quieren**.\n\nTo avoid repeating a noun you already know, use **lo, la, los, las** before the verb:\n\n- el libro → **Lo quiero.**\n- la camisa → **La quiero.**\n- los zapatos → **Los quiero.**\n- las camisas → **Las quiero.**\n\nThe adjective agrees with the noun: la camisa is **cara**, el libro is **caro**. The opposite is **barato** or **barata**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Lo, la, los, las and agreement",
     "texto": [
      "When it is already clear which thing you mean, **lo, la, los, las** replace it and go **before the verb**:\n\n- masculine singular: **lo** (el libro → **lo** quiero)\n- feminine singular: **la** (la camisa → **la** quiero)\n- masculine plural: **los** (los zapatos → **los** quiero)\n- feminine plural: **las** (las camisas → **las** quiero)\n\nThe price verb agrees too: one thing, **cuesta**; several things, **cuestan**. And the adjective changes with the noun: **caro, cara, baratos, baratas**."
     ],
